{
 "section_summary": "The section opens with the concluding portion of an illustrated 1939 issue of the magazine Brasil-Japão, containing articles, letters, advertisements, and reports promoting Japanese-Brazilian cultural and commercial relations. It then includes two State Department cross-reference sheets concerning prospective Japanese industrial projects in Brazil, followed by an American consular despatch transmitting a pamphlet from the Japan Foreign Trade Federation. The enclosed pamphlet advocates expanded Japanese-Brazilian trade, defends Japan’s economic expansion into China, and emphasizes the efficiency and competitiveness of Japanese industry.",
